  KEYWORDS = {Security awareness training, Security breaches, Technology organization},
  LANGUAGE = {English},
  ABSTRACT = {The problem addressed in the study is that there is a rise in security breaches in organizations due to employee vulnerabilities in an information technology organization. Based on this problem, the central research question asked, what if any relationship existed between cybersecurity-employee vulnerabilities and the reduction of security breaches in an information technology organization? The quantitative method employing the association and correlation designs was used to assess data collected from 100 United States participants from the Employee Vulnerability survey. The findings showed that management believed security awareness training (p{\textless}0.001, V = 0.478), policies (p{\textless}0.001, V = 0.495), standard operating procedures (SOPs) (p{\textless}0.001, V = 0.363), and security culture (p = 0.030, V = 0.317) were related to decreased security breaches. The value of information governance, social engineering training, and information security training on reduction in security breaches should be further explored. These findings highlight the importance of incorporating security awareness training, policies, and SOPs into a robust security program aimed at reducing security breaches. A security culture is also an essential component in reducing security breaches.},
